 ## Semantics
 
-Bind an existing selected instance or read its bound Property; it creates nothing. A variable introduced by a standalone typed instance selector such as `Kind//$x;` remains in scope for following statements in the same CFEL fenced block. A variable introduced in an IF condition is in scope within that condition and its matching THEN group only; it is not in scope in following statements. If an outer variable is already bound, a new binding inside IF must use a different variable name; references to the outer variable retain its existing identity.
+Bind an existing selected instance or read its bound Property; it creates nothing. `$x[<Kind>, (conditions)]` binds a named participant selected by a declared Model kind and grouped conditions; `$<Kind>` selects an anonymous instance without providing a reusable name. Conditions are evaluated against the selected participant. A kind reference and its Format do not create the selected instance. The source Claim must identify whether its selection addresses model entities or instance data; binding does not move a match between those layers. A variable introduced by a standalone typed instance selector such as `Kind//$x;` remains in scope for following statements in the same CFEL fenced block. A variable introduced in an IF condition is in scope within that condition and its matching THEN group only; it is not in scope in following statements. If an outer variable is already bound, a new binding inside IF must use a different variable name; references to the outer variable retain its existing identity.
